+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates the `input` a model authored against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before the executor runs. A call the schema rejects is answered with a `ToolResponse` the model can read and correct within the existing tool-round budget, not with a thrown error that ends the conversation, and input that passes reaches the executor exactly as sent. The validator is `ajv`, added to `dependencies`, compiling the same schema objects that are handed to the providers -- there is no second schema to drift.
+
+## Validation in `execute`
+
+- `execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor; on failure it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: answers a missing required property with a rejection naming it and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L31)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the path and expected type, never the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46), [validated by: rejects a value outside a declared enum, naming the property and the constraint](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L169)).
+- A rejection names the failing property path and the constraint that failed, and carries no property value: tool input is where identifying data enters the engine and the engine redacts nothing today, so nothing from a rejected payload reaches the returned text or any log line ([validated by: keeps the rejected payload values out of the returned text and every log line](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L62)).
+- Input the schema accepts reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once, unlisted extra properties included -- nothing is added, coerced or defaulted ([validated by: passes a schema-valid call carrying an unlisted extra property through to the executor unchanged, exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L85)).
+- Validation is configured to enforce those constraints only: it does not inject `additionalProperties: false`, coerce types or apply defaults, and carries no opt-out.
+- `execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` for an unregistered name -- a name the registry does not know is a caller error, not model input to correct ([validated by: still throws Unknown tool for an unregistered name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L196)).
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at `register` time: an uncompilable schema throws at registration with a message naming the tool, so a broken schema fails at startup rather than mid-conversation, and the calls that follow are served by the schema compiled then ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L102), [validated by: serves ten execute calls from the schema compiled at register without reading the schema again](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L117)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is resolved on each call and validated against the schema current at that call, cached by the resolved schema object ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L144)).
+
+## A rejection in the tool loop
+
+- A rejection reaches the model as a tool result rather than as a thrown error, so `processMessage` resolves, the provider reads the rejection text on its next round, and a corrected retry is answered normally; `DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS` is the bound that stops a retry cycle from spinning ([validated by: carries a rejected tool call back to the model as a tool result and resolves on the corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L56)).
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Validating tool *output*; hallucination detection and an evaluation harness; per-tool authorisation -- a schema-valid call for someone else's data is still valid, and authorisation is a separate `ToolContext` boundary concern; retry, timeout and rate limiting around tool execution.
+- Returning an unknown tool name to the model instead of throwing -- the same failure class handled the opposite way, an intentional split tracked as its own issue.
+- The one-line doc comment on `execute` pointing at this spec, and the contract restated in `docs/adding-a-tool.md`, `README.md` and `.specify/spec.md` -- prose for review to judge, not for a test to cite.
+- The validator landing in `package.json` `dependencies` and `npm run build && node --input-type=module -e "import('./dist/index.js')"` exiting `0` -- CI's build, changelog and packaging gates cover these.
